Conclusion:
This lab demonstrated how a SQL injection vulnerability in a login mechanism can be used to bypass authentication and obtain administrator access.
The exercise also provided practical experience with manually interacting with a web application at the HTTP level
The key security lesson is that user-controlled input must never be allowed to alter the structure of an SQL query. Parameterized queries and proper database privilege management are fundamental defenses against SQL injection.
